.TH TUINK 1 "November 2026" "TUInk @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tuink \- terminal text editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tuink
.RI [ options ]
.RB [ \-\- ]
.RI [ file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tuink
is a terminal text editor with syntax highlighting, search, multiple tabs,
and gutter markers for changes since opening or saving a file.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-mouse
Disable mouse tracking and mouse interactions.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-alt\-screen
Do not use the alternate screen buffer.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-color
Render without ANSI colors.
.TP
.BR \-\-theme= name
Select the UI palette: blue, cyan, or light.
.TP
.BR \-\-read
Start in reading mode with editing disabled.
.TP
.BR \-\-open\-as= encoding
Choose the input decoder for this open request: auto, utf-8, utf-16le,
utf-16be, windows-1251, cp866, or koi8-r.
The separated form, for example \fB\-\-open\-as cp866 file.txt\fR, is also accepted.
Specific decoders require an existing file; auto retains ordinary file creation.
UTF-8 preserves an optional BOM. UTF-16LE and UTF-16BE require the matching BOM.
CP866 and KOI8-R must be selected explicitly; automatic detection does not guess them.
.TP
.BR \-\-open\-as\-utf16le
Interpret the selected BOM-marked file as UTF-16LE for this open request only.
Use this for UTF-16LE files whose leading NUL makes their bytes ambiguous with UTF-32LE.
.TP
.BR \-\-profile
Log render timings to standard error.
.TP
.BR \-\-profile\-file= path
Write render timings to a file and enable profiling.
.TP
.BR \-\-file\-uri= uri
Open an absolute ASCII file URI with percent-encoded filename bytes.
Use this option or the file picker for non-UTF-8 Unix filenames and literal U+FFFD names.
Ordinary command-line file and profile paths containing U+FFFD are rejected to avoid selecting another file after native argument decoding.
.TP
.BR \-\-ui= tui
Select the terminal interface. The GUI target is not implemented.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show command-line help.
.TP
.BR \-\-version
Show the application version and exit without opening the terminal or reading settings and recovery data.
.TP
.BR \-\-
End option parsing. The following argument is a literal file path, even if it starts with a dash.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/tuink/tuink.properties
Per-user UI settings by default. An absolute, nonempty XDG_CONFIG_HOME selects
XDG_CONFIG_HOME/tuink/tuink.properties instead. Recovery data is kept in the
same profile's tuink/recovery directory.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/tuink/save-locks-v1
Persistent per-user locks coordinating document and settings saves across profiles.
